OL,3,GNEWSA'Dad was different when he
OL,4,Areturned from Aberfan'
OL,5,
OL,6,FMemories of the Aberfan disaster still
OL,7,Fcast a shadow over a Herefordshire
OL,8,Ffamily 60 years on, with a woman
OL,9,Frecalling how her father was
OL,10,F"different" after helping at the scene.
OL,12,FWednesday marked six decades since a
OL,13,Fcolliery spoil tip collapsed onto the
OL,14,FWelsh mining village, engulfing
OL,15,FPantglas Junior School and nearby homes
OL,16,Fand killing 144 people. Of those who
OL,17,Fdied, 116 were children.
OL,19,FLynne Hunter was seven years old and
OL,20,Fliving in Ross-on-Wye when her father,
OL,21,FEric Owen, a police officer, was called
OL,22,Fto help with the rescue effort.
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
